THE DEFECT
  `renderedRuleTwoRows` is `SPOOL_DERIVATION_INPUT_DISCLOSURE` filtered by
  `match === "normalized_name"`. That constant is built at
  `packages/collector-cli/src/hook-spool.ts` by spreading
  `SPOOL_PROTECTED_IDENTITY_KEYS` — the same array `derivedRuleTwoNames` is
  `[...]`-copied from. So the "rendered == derived" leg of the three-way
  equality is "derived == hand list" told a second time, and cannot red while
  the first leg is green. Nothing in the proof read the PAGE the disclosure
  exists to produce.

THE NEW LEG
  `r_the_privacy_pages_rendered_rule_two_table_names_the_hand_list`
  reads the rule-2 names back out of the rendered markdown table, twice: from
  `renderPrivacySpec(collectPrivacySpecModel())` — the exact call
  `pnpm docs:privacy` makes — and from the committed `docs/privacy-spec.md`.
  Both are compared with `SPOOL_RULE_TWO_DISCLOSED_CANONICAL_NAMES`, which is
  typed by hand and derived from nothing.

