READING
  In all three controls `r_every_protected_identity_name_is_blanked_or_declared`
  stays GREEN with `ruleTwoRenderedRows: 11` — reporting eleven rows from the key
  array while the page prints five or none. That is the restated leg being unable
  to fail, measured. The new check is the only thing that reds.

  `pnpm docs:privacy --check` is not a substitute. It answers "is the committed
  page what the generator renders", which stays true whenever the page is
  regenerated after a generator change — NC-N1c. It never compares the page with
  the hand-written disclosure list. The new leg does, from both sides.
